 ## Verification
 
+- `includes/elementor-compatibility.php` is the single source of explicitly accepted Elementor/Pro version pairs and separate tested evidence for Atomic Interactions and Fragment Cache. Runtime guards, adapters, notices, settings UI and updater gates must consume it; never add independent version rules in PHP/JS, an open-ended range or a filter that widens support. The current schema accepts exact versions only.
+- Every new Elementor/Pro version, including a patch that does not change feature code, requires review, an explicitly updated compatibility declaration and a Kit release before it can be accepted. Do not infer approval from the minor series, mocked version-policy tests or a daily monitor. Record actually tested core/Pro pairs, evidence and acceptance limits separately from approved pairs.
+- Before changing compatibility or releasing, run `php tests/elementor-compatibility.php`, `php tests/elementor-update-guard.php`, and `node tests/elementor-compatibility-drift.cjs`; inspect runtime files for old/scattered guards. Only fixtures/tests/docs may contain reference version declarations outside the registry.
+- The daily compatibility monitor is read-only. It must not change the registry, install/update/purge, commit/push, bump versions or create a release. Notify only on actionable compatibility evidence or a required user decision.
+
 - Run `php -l istodata-utilities.php` when PHP is available.
 - If PHP is not available in PATH, say so explicitly.
 - Check the final changed files and report unrelated pre-existing working tree changes without modifying them.
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,12 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Improve: Centralize Elementor/Pro compatibility declarations and show accepted combinations separately from tested evidence.
+- Tweak: Atomic Interactions compatibility accepts the documented Elementor 4.3.2 / Pro 4.3.0 and tested 4.3.3 / Pro 4.3.1 pairs; each new patch requires review and a Kit compatibility update instead of automatic acceptance within 4.3.x.
+- Fix: Restore Atomic interaction styles after Motion scroll-timeline teardown when entering an excluded breakpoint.
+- Improve: Accept the tested Elementor 4.3.3 / Pro 4.3.1 pair for Fragment Cache; preserve native rendering for graphs with Atomic interactions while allowing independent static fragments alongside Atomic Widgets.
+- New: Block Elementor/Pro WordPress updates only for incompatible active Atomic or opted-in Fragment Cache features, with a protected explicit override for one specific update; keep available updates visible and bypass unsupported runtime features with notices.
+- Fix: Apply the compatibility gate to WordPress bulk and AJAX plugin updates, whose per-plugin hooks omit the update type and action.
 - New: Optional Elementor widget fragment cache with early render bypass, 24-hour default TTL, cross-page reuse, device/WPML variants, template-source invalidation and per-element purge. Off by default; reviewed Template/Mega Menu/Loop Grid/Classic Posts graphs are supported and uncertain technical contexts bypass.
 - Improve: Elementor Device Visibility now removes hidden widget and container branches before frontend rendering, avoiding their PHP widget work where builder content data is available.
 - Tweak: Shortened the Atomic Interactions breakpoint fix setting description.
